<title>SINGAPORE: Esso maintains 15 pct cut at Singapore refinery.</title>
<headline>Esso maintains 15 pct cut at Singapore refinery.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Esso Singapore Private Limited, an affiliate of U.S. oil giant Exxon Corp is still maintaining a 15-percent cut at its 230,000 barrel-per-day (bpd) refinery, a company spokesman said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>He said there were no plans to restore output to normal capacity.</p>
<p>Esso is the only Singapore refinery has yet to restore operations to maximum capacity since refining margins improved more than a week ago.</p>
<p>Poor refinery margins prompted Esso to cut runs by 15 percent in early July.  </p>
<p>Two other refiners, Mobil Oil Singapore and Shell Singapore, which had also reduced runs, resumed full producing at full capacity last week, spokesmen at the two refiners said earlier.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703086)</p>
